## 📱 Core Features

### Owner Voice Recognition

Chill will allow the owner to enroll their voice and later be recognized by the assistant.

Example enrollment phrases:

```text
“Hey Chill, this is my voice.”
“Hey Chill, unlock my assistant.”
“Hey Chill, remember me.”
“Hey Chill, keep my data private.”
“Hey Chill, start listening.”
```

### Consent-First Onboarding

Before voice enrollment, Chill will ask for:

```text
Microphone permission
Explicit voice biometric consent
Clear explanation of data usage
```

### Fallback Authentication

Voice recognition alone is not enough for sensitive actions.

Chill will support fallback methods such as:

```text
PIN
Device biometric
Explicit confirmation
```

### Privacy Controls

Users should be able to:

```text
Delete their voice profile
Withdraw consent
Re-enroll their voice
See what data is stored
```

---

## 🧠 How Voice Recognition Works

Chill’s owner recognition is based on **speaker verification**, not just speech-to-text.

High-level flow:

```text
User speaks
    ↓
Voice activity detection
    ↓
Audio quality check
    ↓
Speaker embedding extraction
    ↓
Comparison with enrolled owner voiceprint
    ↓
Accept, reject, or ask for fallback
```

Planned technologies:

```text
Speaker verification:
- ECAPA-TDNN
- SpeechBrain
- WeSpeaker

Voice activity detection:
- Silero VAD
- WebRTC VAD

Speech-to-text later:
- Whisper
- Vosk
- Cloud STT options
```

---

## 🔐 Security Model

Chill follows a layered security model.

```text
Layer 1: App profile ownership
Layer 2: Voice owner recognition
Layer 3: PIN or OS biometric fallback
Layer 4: Strong confirmation for high-risk actions
```

High-risk actions may require additional verification, such as:

```text
Deleting account
Deleting voice data
Changing security settings
Accessing sensitive personal data
Performing payments
Executing dangerous automation
```

Chill will not claim that voice recognition is 100% secure.

Voice can be affected by:

```text
Background noise
Similar voices
Recordings
AI-generated voice
Poor microphone quality
```

Because of this, Chill uses voice recognition as a convenience and personalization layer.

---

## 🧾 Privacy Principles

Voice data is sensitive biometric data.

Chill is designed around these principles:

```text
Explicit consent before enrollment
Clear purpose explanation
Minimal data collection
No selling of voice data
Deletion option
Secure storage
No hidden background listening
```

Default rule:

```text
Do not store raw audio recordings by default.
Store encrypted voice embeddings when backend support is added.
```

