## 🚀 Getting Started

This project is currently in the scaffold phase.

Once the mobile app is generated inside `apps/mobile`, run:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/sripavan098-creator/chill.git
cd chill/apps/mobile
npm install
npx expo start
```

Then scan the QR code using:

```text
Expo Go on Android
Expo Go on iOS
```

If you are developing on a Chromebook, you can use:

```text
GitHub Codespaces
OpenHands Cloud
Browser-based GitHub editor
```

---

## 🧪 Development Workflow

This project uses a branch-based GitHub workflow.

```text
main
  ↑
Pull Request
  ↑
Feature branch
```

Recommended branch names:

```text
feat/onboarding
feat/voice-enrollment
fix/audio-permission
docs/readme-update
```

Do not push directly to `main`.

Use pull requests and squash merges where possible.

---

## 🤖 AI Agent Rules

This repository is designed to be developed with AI coding agents such as:

```text
OpenHands
GitHub Copilot
GitHub Codespaces
Other browser-based coding agents
```

All agents must follow:

```text
AGENTS.md
docs/PRD.md
docs/SECURITY.md
docs/PRIVACY.md
design/DESIGN.md
```

Key rules:

```text
No hidden background listening
No raw audio storage by default
No voice-only high-risk actions
No misleading security claims
No unnecessary dependencies
No direct pushes to main
```

---

## ⚠️ Disclaimer

Chill is under active development.

Voice recognition is not guaranteed to be perfect and should not be used as the only security mechanism for sensitive operations.

Biometric data processing may be subject to legal requirements depending on your region, including privacy and data protection laws.

